{{!-- The Inbox (`/`, routes/inbox.js + services/inbox.js): replies and mentions from the Inbox's start as conversation cards, drawn
      exactly as a conversation is (partials/thread.hbs): what they answered as the seed, their posts and your replies
      as chat. Tabs: Waiting / Done / All; a search, a sort, pages (the listing engine Your people
      uses: partials/list-search.hbs, partials/pager.hbs). Every post opens on X. Done is a button you press on each
      card ("Mark done" / Reopen, models/InboxMark.js): a like or a reply doesn't move a card. public/js/
      post-actions.js does it in place: the card folds out of the tab it no longer belongs in, and the counts move.
      THE RAIL (wide screens only): who in this tab and search still has a like or a reply coming from you, and how
      many (services/inbox.js railOf), closest first; a name narrows the list to their cards (`?person=`), Everyone
      clears it. Its numbers move as you like, answer and mark done (data-count="rail-<id>", post-actions.js). The
      title spans the top; the rail starts level with the tabs (app.css .inbox-page). --}}
{{!-- `listing`: the plain Waiting list (a phone shows the people / posts and hides the cards); `drilled`: one person or
      one post picked (a phone shows their cards and a way back, never the rail). The desktop draws both as before. --}}
{{> live-pill text="new" list="inbox"}}
{{> owed-model}}
<div class="inbox-page{{#if (or list.person list.post)}} drilled{{else if (eq list.show "waiting")}} listing{{/if}}">
<header class="page-head">
  {{#if (or list.person list.post)}}<p class="inbox-back"><a href="{{everyoneHref}}">{{> icon-back}}Inbox</a>{{#if picked}}<span class="inbox-back-who">{{> avatar person=picked}}<b>{{displayName picked}}</b></span>{{/if}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{!-- THE BREAKDOWN (one big count looked daunting; it's likes and replies, so both, adding up to it):
        every card's likes and replies still owed (inbox.owedTotals), together the sidebar's Inbox count (in the
        accent). post-actions.js moves them as you like, answer and mark done. --}}
  <div class="inbox-title"><h1>Inbox</h1>{{#if (gt (add owed.like owed.reply) 0)}}<p class="owed-split">{{#if likesKnown}}<span class="owed-like">{{> icon-heart}}<b data-count="owe-like">{{count owed.like}}</b><span class="owed-word"> to like</span></span>{{/if}}<span class="owed-reply">{{> icon-reply}}<b data-count="owe-reply">{{count owed.reply}}</b><span class="owed-word"> to reply</span></span></p>{{/if}}{{#if headSwitch}}{{> page-switch headSwitch}}{{/if}}</div>
  {{!-- No subtitle under the title; only when X hasn't granted
        what the ♥ and the reply need: a LINK to /auth/x (form-action 'self' would block a form ending on x.com). --}}
  {{#if regrant}}<p class="note"><a href="/auth/x">Sign in with X again</a> to {{#if regrant.pictures}}reply with photos, GIFs and videos{{else}}like and reply{{/if}} from here.</p>{{/if}}
</header>
{{!-- By person or BY POST: the toggle at the rail's top; Posts lists each card still owing something by what it's about
      (inbox.railOfPosts), most owed first, and picking one shows that card alone (`?post=`), nothing folded. --}}
<nav class="rail{{#if byPosts}} by-posts{{/if}}" aria-label="{{#if likesKnown}}Likes and replies{{else}}Replies{{/if}} to send, by {{#if byPosts}}post{{else}}person{{/if}}">
  <div class="seg-tabs rail-modes">{{#each railModes}}<a href="{{href}}"{{#if on}} class="on" aria-current="true"{{/if}}>{{label}} <span class="seg-n" data-count="rail-mode-{{key}}">{{count n}}</span></a>{{/each}}</div>
  {{!-- THE COLUMNS (one number beside ♥ and ✓ read as if it counted both the like and the reply): each
        row, a person's or a post's (the same controls at both levels), says what it owes the way the head does, ↩ N · ♥
        N, and has its presses, ♥ and ✓, one click each:
        partials/rail-row.hbs. The first row, Everyone / Every post, is THE row too (`rail.everyone`, key "all"): the
        columns' totals, its ♥ the whole view's bulk like, its ✓ Mark all done in two clicks (its ♥ once
        looked pressable and wasn't). --}}
  {{#> rail-row rail.everyone}}<span class="rail-all" aria-hidden="true">{{#if @root.byPosts}}{{> icon-inbox}}{{else}}{{> icon-people}}{{/if}}</span><span class="rail-name">{{#if @root.byPosts}}Every post{{else}}Everyone{{/if}}</span>{{/rail-row}}
  {{!-- ON A PHONE THIS IS THE INBOX (a main screen of the people or posts, each drilled into):
        each row a card, the name and when on its first line (the name never gives way), their newest reply still
        owed under it (as X's notifications summarise, `latest`), what's owed and the presses at its foot, in the same
        place on every row (controls used by the dozen must never move).
        The time and the preview show only there (app.css, the phone's .inbox-page.listing). --}}
  {{#each rail.rows}}
    {{#> rail-row}}{{#if about}}{{> avatar person=about.author}}<span class="rail-text"><span class="rail-head"><span class="rail-name rail-post">{{about.text}}</span>{{#if at}}<time class="rail-time" datetime="{{at}}">{{rel at}}</time>{{/if}}</span></span>{{else}}{{> avatar person=who}}<span class="rail-text"><span class="rail-head"><span class="rail-name">{{displayName who}}</span>{{#if at}}<time class="rail-time" datetime="{{at}}">{{rel at}}</time>{{/if}}</span>{{#if latest.text}}<span class="rail-preview">{{latest.text}}</span>{{/if}}</span>{{/if}}{{/rail-row}}
  {{/each}}
  {{#unless rail.rows.length}}<p class="note rail-empty">Nothing waiting. Inbox zero ✓</p>{{/unless}}
</nav>
{{!-- Not deferred: a phone's list is newest first, ordered before it paints (public/js/rail-order.js). --}}
<script src="/js/rail-order.js?v={{assetV}}"></script>
<div class="rail-main">

<div class="list-head">
  <nav class="seg-tabs" aria-label="Show">
    {{#each tabs}}<a href="{{href}}"{{#if on}} class="on" aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}} <span class="seg-n" data-count="tab-{{key}}">{{count n}}</span></a>{{/each}}
  </nav>
  {{!-- Where you are in the list ("1–20 of 343"); nothing at all when nothing matches (it said "None", which read like
        a control). Every number a press changes in place carries data-count="<name>" (and a word
        that agrees with it, data-plural): public/js/post-actions.js moves them together as a card leaves the list. --}}
  {{!-- On a phone it hides: the tab's own count says it (the head wrapped on a phone). --}}
  {{#if list.matched}}<span class="toolbar-count" data-list-count>{{count list.from}}–<span data-count="list-to">{{count list.to}}</span> of <span data-count="list-matched">{{count list.matched}}</span>{{#if list.q}} matching “{{list.q}}”{{/if}}</span>{{/if}}
</div>

{{!-- Two rows: the head says where you are (the tabs, how many), the toolbar holds what you can do (search, sort, and
      on Waiting, Mark all done). On a phone the search takes its own line and the sort and Mark all share the next. --}}
<div class="toolbar">
  {{!-- No Replies / Mentions filter (removed: it wasn't useful): a card says when it only tagged you. --}}
  {{> list-search action="/" placeholder="Search names and posts" q=list.q sorts=sorts keep=keep}}
  {{!-- THE INBOX'S WINDOW (routes/inbox.js /inbox/within): a setting kept on the account, not a filter in the address
        (it holds on every visit, and the red count follows it), so its own small POST form, saved on change. --}}
  <form class="inbox-within" method="post" action="/inbox/within">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}">
    <select name="within" aria-label="Which replies" data-auto-submit>
      <option value=""{{#unless account.inboxWithin}} selected{{/unless}}>All replies</option>
      <option value="1d"{{#if (eq account.inboxWithin "1d")}} selected{{/if}}>Last 24 hours</option>
    </select>
  </form>
  {{!-- ♥ Like, then ✓ Done, in the order a card has them, to be consistent. --}}
  {{!-- Only for MORE THAN ONE card (with one card, the presses showed twice):
        with one, the toolbar's presses are that card's own head's, the same press twice. post-actions.js leftList
        removes them when presses bring the list down to one. --}}
  {{#if (gt list.matched 1)}}{{> like-all}}{{/if}}
  {{!-- Mark all done: every Waiting card this view matches (its search, every page), up to the newest the page knew
        of (`upTo`); in the rail's person view just their replies (routes/inbox.js done-all). Over the whole view (no
        person or post picked) THE CLICK-AGAIN CONFIRM (it used to ask in THE modal), however many it marks; in a
        person's view one click. Its toast's Undo puts every mark back (models/InboxUndo.js). Without script the button
        sends it directly. --}}
  {{#if (eq list.show "waiting")}}{{#if (gt list.matched 1)}}
    <form class="all-done" id="all-done-form" method="post" action="/inbox/done-all" data-done-all>
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{list.q}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="person" value="{{list.person}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="post" value="{{list.post}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="by" value="{{list.by}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="upTo" value="{{upTo}}">
      {{!-- "Mark N replies done" in the People view, "Mark N posts done" in the Posts view (partials/done-unit.hbs,
            routes/inbox.js doneUnit); a press says "Mark", ✓ Done is the finished state ("Done" on both, differing only by background, was confusing); whose they are, its question says. ONE span
            around the words: a .btn
            is a flex box with a gap, so loose words and spans are each a flex item. --}}
      <button type="submit" class="btn done-btn"{{#unless (or list.person list.post)}} data-confirm="Click again to mark all done"{{/unless}}><span>Mark {{> done-unit}} done</span></button>
    </form>
  {{/if}}{{/if}}
</div>

{{#if threadFollow}}{{> thread-follow}}{{/if}}

{{#if list.rows.length}}
  <div class="threads" data-inbox-show="{{list.show}}">
    {{#each list.rows}}
      {{!-- Replies open under each message (THE POST FOOT, partials/post-foot.hbs: ♥ · ↻ · Reply · On X); the card's ♥ Like N
            and Done sit at its top right (partials/card-presses.hbs), so a card has no foot. No link to the
            conversation's own page (it showed the same view): the card IS the conversation, and their
            name or picture opens their People page. --}}
      {{> thread inboxCard=true}}
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  <div data-list-pager>{{> pager pager}}</div>
{{/if}}
{{!-- The empty list's words, drawn always: hidden while there are cards, shown by post-actions.js when the last one
      on the page leaves and nothing else matches (so the words live here, once). --}}
<p class="note" data-list-empty{{#if list.rows.length}} hidden{{/if}}>{{#if list.q}}Nothing matches “{{list.q}}”.{{else if (eq list.show "waiting")}}{{#if list.post}}Nothing waiting in this one. <a href="{{everyoneHref}}">Every post</a>{{else if picked}}Nothing waiting from {{displayName picked}}. <a href="{{everyoneHref}}">Everyone</a>{{else}}Nothing waiting. Inbox zero ✓{{/if}}{{else}}Nothing here yet.{{/if}}</p>
{{!-- LOAD EARLIER REPLIES (routes/inbox.js; services/inboxStart.js): a new Inbox opens with its newest 20 replies;
      this, at the foot of the last page, brings in the next ones before them. --}}
{{#if more}}<form class="inbox-more" id="inbox-more" method="post" action="/inbox/more" data-busy><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}"><input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{more.back}}"><button type="submit" class="btn">Load {{more.n}} earlier {{plural more.n "reply" "replies"}}</button></form>{{/if}}
</div>
</div>
